// straight to ImRenderer<BrnGraphics::WorldTexturedVertex>::Construct by
// BrnGraphics::Im3dTexPlusLighting::Construct. Being Xenos microcode inside the
// guest image, nothing in the converted asset tree supplies a PC counterpart.
//
// These two arrays are the SAME two programs re-authored for D3D9 from the
// Xenos disassembly (tools/assets/shaders/ctab.py for the register-pinned
// constant names, tools/assets/shaders/xenos.py for the two 22-slot
// instruction streams; the listing is reproduced at the head of
// brn_worldtex.fx). The recovered constant layout is reproduced exactly by the
// recompile: gaWorldTransforms c0 x128, gViewProjection c128 x4, gEyeLocation
// c132 x1 in the vertex program; gLightDirection c0, gLightColour c1,
// gShinyParams c2, DiffuseSampler s0 in the pixel program. No visual oracle was
// used.
//
// Build recipe (identical to tools/assets/shaders/convert_shaders_bundle.py ::
// compile_entry; /Zpr row-major packing is load-bearing):
//     fxc /nologo /T vs_3_0 /E vs_main /O2 /Zpr /Fo worldtex_vs.fxo brn_worldtex.fx
//     fxc /nologo /T ps_3_0 /E ps_main /O2 /Zpr /Fo worldtex_ps.fxo brn_worldtex.fx
// then wrapped by tools/assets/shaders/shader_transcode.py ::
// build_pc_program_buffer(bytecode, shader_type) into platform-4
// ShaderProgramBuffer primary images (0x14-byte ProgramBufferData header +
// D3D9 bytecode at +0x14 + 8-byte ProgramVariableDescriptor table rebuilt from
// the bytecode's CTAB + interned NUL name strings). Only the primary is
// carried: muMicrocodePart3 is 0, there is no Xenos physical block.
//
// Provenance:
//     fxc.exe   Windows SDK 10.0.26100.0 x64
